==German==

===Etymology===
An originally [[Low German|Low]] and [[Central German]] word from {{etyl|gml|de}} {{m|gml|nütlik|nǖtlīk}} (“delicious, delicate”) and late {{etyl|gmh|de}} (Central German) {{m|gmh|nītlīche}}, {{m|gmh|niethlīchen||eagerly}}, from {{etyl|osx|de}} {{m|osx|niudlīko||eagerly}} (compare {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|nēodlīċe}}), derived from {{etyl|osx|de}} {{m|osx|niud}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*neudaz||desire, drive, urge}}. More at {{l|en|needly}}.

